{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Finding the Unknown"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 12:** Ramesh and Suresh have 60 marbles between them. Ramesh has 30 more marbles than Suresh. How many marbles does each boy have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.151,
            0.546,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "In this problem, we have two unknowns. If we denote the number of marbles with Ramesh as x and the number of marbles with Suresh as y, then what are the different equations that we have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.271,
            0.525,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "1. The total number of marbles is 60."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.292,
            0.397,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "x + y = 60.",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.563,
            0.138,
            0.935,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.32,
            0.604,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "2. Ramesh has 30 marbles more than Suresh."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.341,
            0.548,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "x = y + 3 0 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.38,
            0.471,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.311,
                0.499,
                0.373,
                0.515
              ],
              "content": "Suresh"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.373,
            0.787,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.526,
            0.846,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": "How do we find the unknowns using these equations? So far, we have only developed a strategy to solve an equation with one unknown! To get such an equation, we can do the following."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.588,
            0.847,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": "Denote the number of marbles with Suresh as y, and the number of marbles with Ramesh as y + 30."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.626,
            0.783,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "Since the total number of marbles is 60, we have the equation:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.417,
            0.646,
            0.576,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "y+(y+30)=60",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.669,
            0.56,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "2y + 30 = 60.",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.703,
            0.5,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "Use this to find both the unknowns."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.741,
            0.383,
            0.761
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Generating Equations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.765,
            0.847,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "So far, we have solved a given equation to find the value of the letter−number. Can we do the reverse — write equations using a given value of the letter−number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.837,
            0.778,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "？ Write equations whose solution is y = 5. Share the equations you made with each other and discuss the methods used."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.833,
            0.904,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
        {
